      "Turn-flow example: 1. Deal: 13 cards each, counterclockwise; dealer may cut but not shuffle after first deal. 2. Bidding: From dealer's right, each player speaks once (pass/ter/behi ter or bid 8-13 tricks or double 13). Highest bidder is declarer, chooses trump, leads first trick with a trump. 3. Play: Follow suit; winner of trick leads next. Play ends when declarer's side makes or loses the bid. 4. Scoring: Won bid scores tricks bid; lost bid scores twice that many to opponents. Double 13 scores 26 or 52. First to 104 wins.",
